  <activity label="loopex6muc-sgl" xml:id="loopex6muc-sgl" numbered="yes" adaptive="yes" indentation="hide" language="java">
    <statement>
      <p>
        The main method in the following class should print 3 rows with 6 *’s in
        each row. But, the blocks have been mixed up and include extra blocks that are not needed in a correct solution. Drag the needed blocks from
        the left and put them in the correct order on the right. Click the Check
        button to check your solution.
      </p>
    </statement>

    <blocks>
      <block order="10">
        <cline>public class Test1</cline>
        <cline>{</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="7">
        <cline>    public static void main(String[] args)</cline>
        <cline>    {</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="1">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Use an outer for loop that runs 3 times, once per row</cline>
          <cline>        for (int x = 3; x &gt; 0; x--)</cline>
          <cline>        {</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Use an outer for loop that runs 3 times, once per row</cline>
          <cline>        for (int x = 0; x &lt;= 3; x++)</cline>
          <cline>        {</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="2">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>            // Use an inner for loop that runs 6 times for each row</cline>
          <cline>            for (int y = 6; y &gt; 0; y--)</cline>
          <cline>            {</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>            // Use an inner for loop that runs 6 times for each row</cline>
          <cline>            for (int y = 0; y &lt;= 6; y++)</cline>
          <cline>            {</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>            // Use an inner for loop that runs 6 times for each row</cline>
          <cline>            for (int y = 6; y &gt; 0; y--);</cline>
          <cline>            {</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="4">
        <cline>                 // Print a star without moving to a new line</cline>
        <cline>                 System.out.print("*");</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="8">
        <cline>            } // end inner for loop</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="3">
        <cline>            // Move to a new line after the row is done</cline>
        <cline>            System.out.println();</cline>
        <cline>        } // end outer for loop</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="6">
        <cline>    } // end main method</cline>
        <cline>} // end of class</cline>
      </block>
    </blocks>
  </activity>

  <activity label="loopex7muc-sgl" xml:id="loopex7muc-sgl" numbered="yes" adaptive="yes" indentation="hide" language="java">
    <statement>
      <p>
        The main method in the following class should print 1 (followed by a
        newline), then 22 (followed by a newline), and then 333 (followed by a
        newline). But, the blocks have been mixed up and include extra blocks that are not needed in a correct solution. Drag the needed blocks from the left
        and put them in the correct order on the right. Click the Check button
        to check your solution.
      </p>
    </statement>

    <blocks>
      <block order="8">
        <cline>public class Test1</cline>
        <cline>{</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="5">
        <cline>    public static void main(String[] args)</cline>
        <cline>    {</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="4">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Use an outer for loop counting rows up from one to three</cline>
          <cline>        for (int x = 1; x &lt;= 3; x++)</cline>
          <cline>        {</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Use an outer for loop counting rows up from one to three</cline>
          <cline>        for (int x = 0; x &lt; 3; x++)</cline>
          <cline>        {</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="7">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>            // Use an inner for loop running as many times as the row number</cline>
          <cline>            for (int y = 0; y &lt; x; y++)</cline>
          <cline>            {</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>            // Use an inner for loop running as many times as the row number</cline>
          <cline>            for (int y = 0; y &lt;= x; y++)</cline>
          <cline>            {</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="1">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>                // Print the row number without moving to a new line</cline>
          <cline>                System.out.print(x);</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>                // Print the row number without moving to a new line</cline>
          <cline>                System.out.print(y);</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="6">
        <cline>            } // end inner for loop</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="3">
        <cline>            // Move to a new line after the row is done</cline>
        <cline>            System.out.println();</cline>
        <cline>        } // end outer for loop</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="2">
        <cline>    } // end main method</cline>
        <cline>} // end of class</cline>
      </block>
    </blocks>
  </activity>

