  <activity label="loopex10muc-sgl" xml:id="loopex10muc-sgl" numbered="yes" adaptive="yes" indentation="hide" language="java">
    <statement>
      <p>
        The <c>even_div(s, n)</c> method in the <c>NumWorker</c> class should
        return the number of digits in <c>s</c> (a string representation of a
        number) that are evenly divisible by <c>n</c>. For example,
        <c>even_div("6892",3)</c> should return 2 since both 6 and 9 are evenly
        divisible by 3. The blocks have been mixed up and include extra blocks
        that are not needed in a correct solution.
      </p>
    </statement>

    <blocks>
      <block order="2">
        <cline>public class NumWorker</cline>
        <cline>{</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="8">
        <cline>    public static int even_div(String s, int n)</cline>
        <cline>    {</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="7">
        <cline>        // Start the count of divisible digits at zero</cline>
        <cline>        int count = 0;</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="13">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Visit each digit in the string in order</cline>
          <cline>        for (int i = 0; i &lt; s.length(); i++)</cline>
          <cline>        {</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Visit each digit in the string in order</cline>
          <cline>        for (int i = 0; i &lt;= s.length(); i++)</cline>
          <cline>        {</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="1">
        <cline>            // Get the digit at this position in the string</cline>
        <cline>            String c_digit = s.substring(i, i+1);</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="5">
        <cline>            // Convert the digit to an integer so you can divide</cline>
        <cline>            int c_num = Integer.parseInt(c_digit);</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="4">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>            // Check for an evenly divisible digit and count it</cline>
          <cline>            if (c_num % n == 0)</cline>
          <cline>            {</cline>
          <cline>                count += 1;</cline>
          <cline>            } // end if</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>            // Check for an evenly divisible digit and count it</cline>
          <cline>            if (c_num / n == 0)</cline>
          <cline>            {</cline>
          <cline>                count += 1;</cline>
          <cline>            } // end if</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="10">
        <cline>        } // end for loop</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="12">
        <cline>        // Return the count of divisible digits after checking every digit</cline>
        <cline>        return count;</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="11">
        <cline>    } // end method even_div</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="6">
        <cline>} // end of class</cline>
      </block>
    </blocks>
  </activity>
</section>
